# L1 / B009 — http-api, httpclient-factory (+resilience), logging (+serilog), modern-csharp, project-structure (+references).

C X29 EX RUN-016,DEP-020 | MUST NOT | Do not wrap normal ORM operations in a generic application-level retry pipeline; use the provider's own execution strategy for transient database faults; HTTP retry policies are not database policies. | database access resilience | none stated | RUN-016 governs when retries are safe and the oracle treats database-retry examples as conditional technique (EXC-007); no oracle policy forbids an application-level retry pipeline around ORM operations. | Wrapping repository calls or SaveChanges in a generic resilience retry pipeline violates the instruction even when the operation is idempotent.
C X30 EX RUN-005 | MUST NOT | Never mutate a shared HttpClient's DefaultRequestHeaders concurrently; apply per-request values such as dynamic tokens per request or through a delegating handler. | outbound HTTP clients | none stated | RUN-005 governs client lifetime; thread-safe header handling is client technique that no oracle policy states. | Setting a per-user access token on DefaultRequestHeaders of a shared typed client per call violates the instruction.
C X31 EX DEP-008,DEP-023 | MUST | global.json pins the intended SDK line: the current stable SDK of the target .NET release (no RC/preview unless explicitly requested) with a rollForward policy that allows normal patch/feature-band servicing. | repository scaffolding and shared .NET configuration | Preview/RC when explicitly requested. | DEP-008 fixes the platform and DEP-023 repository-level build configuration; no oracle policy requires a global.json SDK pin or a specific roll-forward policy. | A scaffolded solution without global.json, or with a pin that blocks feature-band servicing, deviates from the template.

